<text>See also references of EP     1065056A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ENDO HIRONORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ENDO, HIRONORI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ENDO HIRONORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ENDO, HIRONORI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>The timing at which whether or not an ink droplet is ejected from each nozzle is judged is preset at least in two different printing modes out of multiple printing modes that a printer has. Alternatively, different combinations of inspection timings and inspection principles are preset at least in two different modes out of multiple printing modes. When printing is carried out in one printing mode selected from at least the two printing modes, dot skip is inspected at the preset timing in the printing mode according to the inspection principle.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention permet de fixer préalablement le moment auquel une gouttelette d'encre est éjectée ou non de chaque buse selon au moins deux modes d'impression différents, lesquels font partie des multiples modes d'impression d'une imprimante. Dans une variante, diverses combinaisons de moments d'inspection et de principes d'inspection sont fixées préalablement selon au moins deux modes différents faisant partie des multiples modes d'impression d'une imprimante. Lorsque l'impression se déroule selon un mode d'impression choisi parmi au moins deux modes d'impression, les points manquants sont inspectés au moment fixé préalablement selon le mode d'impression, en fonction dudit principe d'inspection.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>